---
title: Example · Sequence diagram
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    actorBkg: "#333333"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#fcd34d"
    labelTextColor: "#000000"
    noteTextColor: "#e0e0e0"
  themeCSS: |
    /* database · db */
    g.actor[transform] path { fill: #1c2f4a; stroke: #93c5fd; }
    /* queue */
    g.actor g[transform] path { fill: #2e2650; stroke: #c4b5fd; }
    /* database label clears the cylinder */
    g.actor[transform] + text { transform: translateY(12px); }
    g.actor[transform] + text tspan { paint-order: stroke; stroke: #1f1f1f; stroke-width: 6px; }
    /* collections · file */
    rect.actor:not([rx]) { fill: #3d3415; stroke: #fcd34d; }
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 80
    width: 200
    wrap: true
---
%% Behavior authority: <domain>.md.
%% Participant `type`: `boundary` (entry point) · `control` (logic) · `entity` (domain record) · `database` · `queue` · `collections`; `actor` is a person.
%% Arrows: `->>` call · `-->>` reply · `-)` async · `-x` failed · `->` `-->` no head · `<<->>` two-way · `-|\` half head; `()` on either end meets the lifeline centre.
%% `+`/`-` on an arrow, or `activate X` / `deactivate X`, marks execution; `create`/`destroy` bound a participant's life; `link X: label @ url` or `links X: {"label": "url", …}` adds a menu, except on `boundary` · `control` · `entity`, where the whole diagram fails to render.
%% `<<-->>` two-way reply · `--x` failed reply.
%% `create actor D as Name` creates an actor; `#9829;` · `#infin;` entity codes write symbols in message text.
%% Blocks: `critical`/`option` · `loop` · `par`/`and` · `alt`/`else` · `opt` · `break` · `rect rgb(…)` highlight; `autonumber start step`.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber 1 1
  actor User as Customer
  box rgb(36, 36, 36) Order service · system boundary
    participant API@{ "type": "boundary", "alias": "Order API" }
    participant Worker as Fulfilment worker<br/>background
    participant Rules@{ "type": "control", "alias": "Pricing rules" }
  end
  participant Order@{ "type": "entity", "alias": "Order record" }
  participant DB@{ "type": "database", "alias": "Order DB" }
  participant Queue@{ "type": "queue", "alias": "Event queue" }
  participant Logs@{ "type": "collections", "alias": "Audit log" }
  link DB: Runbook @ https://example.com/runbook

  User->>+API: Place order
  API->>API: Validate cart and stock
  API->>()Rules: Price cart
  activate Rules
  Rules-->>API: Total with discounts
  deactivate Rules
  critical Accept transaction
    API->>DB: Insert order
    DB-->Order: Row maps to record
  option Insert fails
    API-->>User: Synchronous error
  end
  API-)Worker: Start fulfilment · no reply awaited
  API-->>-User: Order accepted

  rect rgb(23, 61, 37)
    Note right of Worker: em · the span this diagram explains
    loop Until shipped
      par Record events
        Worker->>Logs: Append fulfilment event
      and Report progress
        Worker-|\Order: Update status
        Order->DB: Persist
      end
    end
  end

  create participant Courier
  Worker->>Courier: Hand over parcel
  Courier<<->>User: Arrange delivery slot
  Courier-->>Worker: Delivered
  destroy Courier
  Worker->>Courier: Close handover

  alt Shipped
    Worker->>Queue: Publish OrderShipped
    Queue--)User: Asynchronous notification
  else Publish rejected
    rect rgb(66, 35, 35)
      Worker-xQueue: Publish rejected · issue
    end
  end

  opt Customer cancels
    User->>API: Cancel order
    break Already shipped
      API-->>User: Return final status
    end
  end

  Note left of User: A single-side note
  Note over API,DB: • A note spanning several participants<br/>• One line per distinct sentence
